{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact 645572a39796b8b57ea974a5886b6496f6fa80ca, sole primary af62176f4a87181937d85ab27ff5a8c9d1767ee1 read first/full. This reviews the design only; it commissions no implementation and approves no dependent evidence-rules design.\n\nF1 — High, sections 2–3 and step 1: a new auto-merge act is not compatible with the present destination. At cited main 8412601d, packages/platform/src/destination-reading.ts:38 reads only an exact signed intent kind \"merge\"; reservation.ts:217–222 requires the merger's current change.merge grant. change.auto-merge alone therefore cannot land. Giving the landing member both grants would also let it invoke ordinary merge without the proposed additional guards unless that route is explicitly fenced. The escalation act separately requires change.edit-any (change.ts:874–875). Describe one complete, bounded authority path, including escalation and the ordinary human path. Either demonstrate an existing-protocol route whose data enforces the separation, or name the versioned destination/host compatibility and grants it needs; do not widen old pinned cohorts. Reclassify the \"data; no deploy; step 1 alone\" claim accordingly.\n\nF2 — Medium, sections 3, 5–6: step 1 claims working confidence from reviews, but step 2 introduces its missing value. Current reviews have verdict/body, not structured confidence (change.ts:103–115). Further, ruleInput exposes named subjects and fetched facts, not all other local review items (guards.ts:109–118); copying merge's subjects does not supply reviews.confidence. Put the advisory confidence form and its bounded, exact-manifest/tree input binding into the minimum confidence slice, or say (c) waits for it. State how an agent may submit that advisory value without receiving ordinary counted change.review approval authority; missing/empty/untrusted confidence or trust must not satisfy automatic landing. The illustrative expression need not become production syntax in