tes. The present destination protocol and the minimum confidence inputs prevent approval of the claimed first slice. The inference that open scopes receive rule values only through a new ask-rules response is supported by change.ts:437–445 and rules-scope.ts:294–306.\n\nSecurity: preserve counted human approvals and the destination's fresh merger authority; an advisory model value is neither a person's approval nor proof of an outside claim. Close the ordinary-merge bypass and make freshness an operative native condition.\n\nSimplification: keep this a short design, with one end-to-end minimum slice, explicit later dependencies and one agreed attempt policy. No generic coordinator or clock/I/O access in JSONata is needed.\n\nValidation: full 138-line candidate and the cited current-source boundaries inspected at 8412601d; exact one-file diff and git diff --check pass. No source changes, package installation, provider calls, deployment, or repeated whole gate for prose. The shared staged See landing was left untouched.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af62176f4a87181937d85ab27ff5a8c9d1767ee1","binding":"assigned","head":"645572a39796b8b57ea974a5886b6496f6fa80ca","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ae9e177c59807e77af9da1a366e11f2174900265\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:64ce9be2beda6cbb28e09aa9de06be70e68a797d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:21c150ba91d0016cd7e945d3de7bf638549dcb1b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}